      "gloss": "the person who rents property"
    },
    {
      "expression": "lessor",
      "gloss": "the person who owns and rents out property"
    },
    {
      "expression": "covenants",
      "gloss": "formal promises or agreements, especially in a contract"
    },
    {
      "expression": "herein",
      "gloss": "in this document or agreement"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "承租人应就因违反本协议中的任何约定而引起的所有索赔，向出租人作出赔偿。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "It is proper for us to think about whether acting in that way fits with what we are obliged to do.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "behoves us",
      "gloss": "it is right or proper for us (to do something)"
    },
    {
      "expression": "such a course of action",
      "gloss": "acting in that particular way"
    },
    {
      "expression": "consonant with",
      "gloss": "in agreement with; matching"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": "The sentence uses a formal, impersonal construction: 'It behoves us to consider...' means 'It is proper for us to consider...'. The 'whether' clause is the object of 'consider', and 'consonant with our obligations' is an adjective phrase describing 'such a course of action'.",
  "translation": "我们应当考虑，这样的做法是否符合我们的义务。"
}
